From 07940541a87630414d567ee0541c526fe9e610b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:54:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/28] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8953: drop HW_CTRL from
 venus_core0_gdsc

The vendor kernel runs Venus on MSM8953 with software power collapse only
(qcom,sw-power-collapse, no hardware trigger on venus-core0). With HW_CTRL
on venus_core0_gdsc the encoder core stalled after about 1.5 s on every
second run, and at QP 51 the whole board hung.

This goes together with "media: venus: use software power collapse only
on MSM8953". Tested on Lenovo ThinkSmart View (APQ8053, Venus firmware
VIDEO.VE.4.2).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c
index c4ec995..de228a7 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c
@@ -3873,7 +3873,6 @@ static struct gdsc venus_core0_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "venus_core0",
 	},
-	.flags = HW_CTRL,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 };
 
